  "notes": "A mercury lamp’s four visible lines (435.8, 546.1, 577.0 and 579.1 nm), collimated, through a 600 l/mm transmission grating blazed for the first order. A 100 mm lens focuses each order and colour to its own point on the screen: the grating is blazed so most of the light goes into the first order, spread by colour; the zero order is weak. The yellow doublet, 2.1 nm apart, lands 0.1 mm apart. Open the screen’s Rays tab and plot power against position to read the spectrum; change the grating’s lines per mm to see the dispersion change."
